course: dictionary
lesson: 14638
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can change its meaning depending on where you find it. Preaching is a good example. In a church, preaching means giving a religious talk. «The preaching lasted twenty minutes, and the whole church listened.» The clues are church and listened, so preaching means the talk itself.
explain: Preaching can also mean the message that is given in the talk. «Her preaching about kindness made everyone think about how they treat others.» Here preaching is the message, the idea being shared, not the act of speaking.
explain: Outside church, preaching can mean something unkind. «Stop preaching at me, Dad!» The clues are stop and the bossy tone, so it means lecturing someone about what is right in an annoying way. Ask yourself who is speaking and how it sounds, then try your meaning in the sentence.
fact: Preaching means giving religious talks, or the message given in those talks.
fact: A preacher is the person who does the preaching.
fact: In everyday talk, preaching can mean telling someone what is right in a bossy, lecturing way.
fact: Context clues such as church, sermon and service point to the religious meaning.
fact: «Preaching to the converted» means trying to convince people who already agree with you.
exercise: «The preacher spoke for twenty minutes about being kind to others.» In this sentence, what is preaching? | A sort of lunch served after a match | A type of song sung in a choir | *Giving a religious talk in church | A loud noise from the playground
exercise: Mum says, «Stop preaching, I already know I should tidy my room!» What does preaching mean here? | *Telling someone what is right in a bossy, lecturing way | Singing loudly in the car | Giving a religious talk in church | The message of a famous book
exercise: Which word in «The church was full for the preaching on Sunday» tells you where the preaching happened? | full | was | Sunday | *church
test: «Her preaching about honesty made the whole class think about what they said.» What is the preaching? | A kind of cake baked for the class | *The message that is preached, the idea about honesty | A football match on Sunday | A loud noise from the hall
test: What does «preaching to the converted» mean? | Giving a talk about religion to people who have never heard of it | Speaking in a very loud voice | *Trying to convince people who already agree with you | Giving a prize to the best speaker
exam: Jamal says, «I'm tired of his preaching.» What does preaching mean here? | The message of a famous speaker | Church talks given every Sunday | *Bossy lecturing about what is right | A slow, sleepy kind of speech
